1
00:00:08,640 --> 00:00:09,877
The world.

2
00:00:09,960 --> 00:00:11,877
What a glorious place.

3
00:00:11,960 --> 00:00:16,117
Seek freedom, and it will lie
stretched out before your eyes.

4
00:00:16,200 --> 00:00:19,340
If the endless dream guides
your restless spirit,

5
00:00:19,660 --> 00:00:23,940
seize it, raise your flag, and stand tall.

6
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:32,717
I think back to the time
when my search first began.

7
00:00:32,800 --> 00:00:35,317
I left behind those shores of sand.

8
00:00:35,400 --> 00:00:38,700
For the endless everlasting
world out there.

9
00:00:39,540 --> 00:00:42,817
I know that with the
burning passion driving me.

10
00:00:42,900 --> 00:00:48,540
Someday, somewhere, I'll finally see the
light I have searched for everywhere?

11
00:00:53,120 --> 00:00:55,757
When the summer sun is shining.

12
00:00:55,840 --> 00:00:58,677
Shaking the sails of my heart, I know.

13
00:00:58,760 --> 00:01:01,580
You're the way from the sea.

14
00:01:02,920 --> 00:01:05,797
A brand new world that has been hiding.

15
00:01:05,880 --> 00:01:08,817
Has opened up its doors for me to go.

16
00:01:08,900 --> 00:01:11,880
You're the way from the sky.

17
00:01:12,900 --> 00:01:15,337
We're in the troubled ways.

18
00:01:15,420 --> 00:01:17,857
From all despair I can be saved.

19
00:01:17,940 --> 00:01:21,177
For the horizon on the other side is.

20
00:01:25,680 --> 00:01:28,697
And though I've traveled far
from where my search began,

21
00:01:28,780 --> 00:01:31,260
over seas of green and shores of sand,

22
00:01:31,360 --> 00:01:34,560
through the endless
everlasting world out there.

23
00:01:35,460 --> 00:01:38,780
I know that with this
burning passion driving me,

24
00:01:39,060 --> 00:01:44,280
some days somewhere I'll finally see
the light I will search for everywhere.

25
00:01:52,440 --> 00:01:54,820
That old lady ratted us out!

26
00:01:55,860 --> 00:01:57,120
She lied to us.

27
00:01:57,280 --> 00:01:59,868
She said it was okay
for us to pass through.

28
00:02:00,040 --> 00:02:03,360
But when we did, they
accused us of illegal entry?

29
00:02:03,960 --> 00:02:05,380
That's flat-out fraud.

30
00:02:06,760 --> 00:02:07,590
Exactly.

31
00:02:07,780 --> 00:02:10,257
But then, even if we were
told we couldn't pass,

32
00:02:10,340 --> 00:02:11,957
we would have just forced our way through.

33
00:02:12,040 --> 00:02:14,377
I mean, how was that little
old lady going to stop us?

34
00:02:14,460 --> 00:02:15,290
Shut up!

35
00:02:15,373 --> 00:02:17,437
In any case, you're in
a great deal of trouble.

36
00:02:17,520 --> 00:02:19,617
You're now second-degree
criminals, and as such,

37
00:02:19,700 --> 00:02:23,077
I'm afraid Conis and I are
unable to assist you any longer.

38
00:02:23,160 --> 00:02:25,866
Why are you talking to
us from way over there?

39
00:02:26,240 --> 00:02:28,593
I really don't see what the big deal is.

40
00:02:28,900 --> 00:02:31,547
I'm surprised you're
not used to this by now.

41
00:02:33,120 --> 00:02:34,591
I've been meaning to ask.

42
00:02:35,060 --> 00:02:37,460
Why'd you come back, Nami? What?

43
00:02:37,740 --> 00:02:39,877
We were finally gonna get to set sail and

44
00:02:39,960 --> 00:02:42,097
head out on an amazing
adventure until you...

45
00:02:42,180 --> 00:02:44,397
I mean, we were about
to come looking for you.

46
00:02:44,480 --> 00:02:45,892
We were getting worried.

47
00:02:46,100 --> 00:02:48,860
I think you and I need
to have a little talk.

48
00:02:50,880 --> 00:02:52,880
Forget about your big adventure!

49
00:02:53,580 --> 00:02:55,200
It's never gonna happen!

50
00:02:56,400 --> 00:02:58,277
You haven't seen what I've seen!

51
00:02:58,360 --> 00:03:01,057
That island is full of the types of
people you don't want to mess with!

52
00:03:01,140 --> 00:03:02,797
I don't care who you think you are!

53
00:03:02,880 --> 00:03:05,637
Granted, we don't know what this
guy is, but his powers are real!

54
00:03:05,720 --> 00:03:08,277
And there's no way I'm ever
going back there again!

55
00:03:08,360 --> 00:03:09,720
So forget it! Got me?

56
00:03:13,440 --> 00:03:16,616
How about you just relax
here while the rest of us go?

57
00:03:16,880 --> 00:03:18,233
We're wanted criminals!

58
00:03:18,380 --> 00:03:20,477
I'm not staying here a
minute longer either!

59
00:03:20,560 --> 00:03:21,390
Are you nuts?

60
00:03:21,473 --> 00:03:22,737
Get your priorities straight!

61
00:03:22,820 --> 00:03:24,877
The adventure is always
the most important part!

62
00:03:24,960 --> 00:03:27,520
My priorities are life first, then honey!

63
00:03:28,520 --> 00:03:30,457
Please tell me I'm third on that list!

64
00:03:30,540 --> 00:03:31,370
Don't push me!

65
00:03:31,760 --> 00:03:33,113
You raise a good point.

66
00:03:33,580 --> 00:03:36,877
We put all of our energy into
just trying to get up here,

67
00:03:36,960 --> 00:03:40,725
but we never really thought about
how we were going to get back.

68
00:03:41,600 --> 00:03:44,365
Is there a safe way back
to the Blue Sea World?

69
00:03:44,680 --> 00:03:46,800
Can we ever even go home again?

70
00:03:47,980 --> 00:03:51,437
There is a way, but at this juncture,
I'm afraid it's no longer safe.

71
00:03:51,520 --> 00:03:54,337
Your only hope for escape is
to make your way to Cloud End.

72
00:03:54,420 --> 00:03:56,640
From there, you can travel home. Huh?

73
00:03:57,080 --> 00:03:58,160
What's Cloud End?

74
00:03:58,440 --> 00:04:00,557
And how are we supposed to get there?

75
00:04:00,640 --> 00:04:02,857
It's a region that lies far to the east.

76
00:04:02,940 --> 00:04:07,293
The only way for you to get there is
to travel across the White White Sea.

77
00:04:07,780 --> 00:04:11,040
OK, so we sell east and
we eventually get home.

78
00:04:11,200 --> 00:04:13,120
But I don't want to go home.

79
00:04:13,840 --> 00:04:17,800
Your other option is stay and get
sentenced to death. Listen to me.

80
00:04:17,980 --> 00:04:21,537
I don't want you causing any more
trouble for Conis and her dad.

81
00:04:21,620 --> 00:04:23,557
No, don't worry about us.

82
00:04:23,640 --> 00:04:27,737
Even if we leave right now, there's no
guarantee we'll make a clean escape.

83
00:04:27,820 --> 00:04:30,857
We don't have any time to
lose, so just get on the ship!

84
00:04:30,940 --> 00:04:34,277
You'll have your big adventure, I promise,
but right now we need to get going!

85
00:04:34,360 --> 00:04:36,595
So come on, everybody, let's set sail!

86
00:04:38,420 --> 00:04:39,777
Thanks for all your help!

87
00:04:39,860 --> 00:04:41,280
We really appreciate it!

88
00:04:43,140 --> 00:04:44,197
Ooh, hold on!

89
00:04:44,280 --> 00:04:45,339
Come on, now what?

90
00:04:45,460 --> 00:04:46,440
Hey, old man!

91
00:04:47,720 --> 00:04:48,779
What is it, Luffy?

92
00:04:48,900 --> 00:04:50,220
Can I ask a favor?

93
00:04:50,620 --> 00:04:52,637
You mind if we take the
leftovers from earlier?

94
00:04:52,720 --> 00:04:53,580
Of course not.

95
00:04:53,760 --> 00:04:54,617
They're all yours.

96
00:04:54,700 --> 00:04:55,530
Woo-hoo!

97
00:04:55,613 --> 00:04:57,277
Come on, Sanji, make us lunch!

98
00:04:57,360 --> 00:04:58,717
I'm glad you got priorities.

99
00:04:58,800 --> 00:05:02,153
In that case, could I ask for
a teensy little favor, too?

100
00:05:03,280 --> 00:05:04,717
You're an engineer, right?

101
00:05:04,800 --> 00:05:08,741
I don't suppose you could spare
any parts or tools to fix our ship.

102
00:05:08,940 --> 00:05:10,640
What's mine is yours, Usopp.

103
00:05:10,780 --> 00:05:12,777
Feel free to take anything you need.

104
00:05:12,860 --> 00:05:13,690
Uh, guys?

105
00:05:13,980 --> 00:05:15,156
Where are you going?

106
00:05:15,860 --> 00:05:16,690
Hello?

107
00:05:16,773 --> 00:05:17,603
They got food!

108
00:05:17,900 --> 00:05:20,977
Tell you what, you go ahead and
ready the ship for departure,

109
00:05:21,060 --> 00:05:23,260
and we'll be back before you know it.

110
00:05:24,500 --> 00:05:26,860
He's dead set on going to that island.

111
00:05:27,940 --> 00:05:29,320
Doesn't he get it?

112
00:05:29,460 --> 00:05:30,777
Don't take it out on us.

113
00:05:30,860 --> 00:05:31,978
You know how he is.

114
00:05:32,420 --> 00:05:33,860
Seriously, try to relax.

115
00:05:35,280 --> 00:05:37,757
Chopper, you're still
on my side, aren't you?

116
00:05:37,840 --> 00:05:38,670
Aren't you?

117
00:05:38,840 --> 00:05:39,920
Don't answer that.

118
00:05:42,640 --> 00:05:43,540
Heavy, quick!

119
00:05:49,740 --> 00:05:52,622
I was about to drop the
ladder for you, you know.

120
00:05:53,860 --> 00:05:56,742
You know there's no
persuading Luffy of anything!

121
00:05:57,120 --> 00:05:59,697
He won't listen, even if
we all gang up on him.

122
00:05:59,780 --> 00:06:02,100
Fine, then I guess I'll just stay put.

123
00:06:02,940 --> 00:06:05,411
Well, you're free to do whatever you want.

124
00:06:05,680 --> 00:06:06,940
I know that!

125
00:06:07,640 --> 00:06:10,420
But if I stay here, I'll be killed!

126
00:06:11,180 --> 00:06:12,010
Yep.

127
00:06:12,260 --> 00:06:13,840
Quite a predicament.

128
00:06:17,060 --> 00:06:17,890
Jerk!

129
00:06:19,600 --> 00:06:22,300
Robin, let's go beat
some sense into Luffy.

130
00:06:22,580 --> 00:06:23,580
Won't work.

131
00:06:25,060 --> 00:06:28,237
I guess we'd have a better
chance against the white berets.

132
00:06:28,320 --> 00:06:32,849
And you know they've already got to be
gathering reinforcements to follow us.

133
00:06:36,840 --> 00:06:38,597
Follow you, idiots.

134
00:06:38,680 --> 00:06:41,660
Inaru and his priest
aren't going anywhere.

135
00:06:42,320 --> 00:06:45,320
Why should I bother when
your true judgment awaits?

136
00:06:45,960 --> 00:06:48,842
Once you weigh anchor,
your challenge will begin.

137
00:06:49,380 --> 00:06:54,100
Your ship will set its own course
to the forbidden sacred grounds.

138
00:06:56,240 --> 00:06:57,820
The Upper Yard.

139
00:07:00,280 --> 00:07:02,700
Mmm, this is really good.

140
00:07:03,220 --> 00:07:05,985
Save some for the trip,
and for the rest of us.

141
00:07:07,260 --> 00:07:10,060
There's plenty here, so I hold back.

142
00:07:10,800 --> 00:07:12,880
This does have to feed all of us!

143
00:07:13,520 --> 00:07:14,417
Conis! Refill!

144
00:07:14,500 --> 00:07:16,265
Why don't you get it yourself?

145
00:07:16,420 --> 00:07:18,200
Speaking of, where is Conis?

146
00:07:18,400 --> 00:07:21,097
I think she went to bid
farewell to the others.

147
00:07:21,180 --> 00:07:23,100
Oh I brought you some more tea!

148
00:07:27,760 --> 00:07:30,777
So you're the shipwright
for your vessel, aren't you?

149
00:07:30,860 --> 00:07:33,357
Well, not really, actually I'm a sniper.

150
00:07:33,440 --> 00:07:35,237
Wow, that sounds exciting!

151
00:07:35,320 --> 00:07:39,849
Yeah, I guess so, but it means we don't
have a regular ship ride in our crew.

152
00:07:40,480 --> 00:07:42,857
Let's see, how can I put this delicately?

153
00:07:42,940 --> 00:07:47,705
I am cursed with supreme skill on every
subject, and the whole crew relies on me!

154
00:07:49,180 --> 00:07:53,533
Yeah, it's a lot of work, but without
me, the ship just wouldn't function.

155
00:07:54,500 --> 00:07:59,000
My official title is sharpshooter,
but I'm also the co-captain.

156
00:07:59,680 --> 00:08:01,857
And that's why everyone calls me...

157
00:08:01,940 --> 00:08:02,860
Captain!

158
00:08:04,200 --> 00:08:08,217
Oh, your color arrangement clearly
denotes the work of a professional.

159
00:08:08,300 --> 00:08:09,160
Of course.

160
00:08:09,380 --> 00:08:11,909
I consider the plating
of food an art form.

161
00:08:12,540 --> 00:08:13,980
No, that doesn't work.

162
00:08:14,260 --> 00:08:15,817
Throws off the whole arrangement.

163
00:08:15,900 --> 00:08:20,237
If I put the red one here and then the
emerald green broad beans across the back...

164
00:08:20,320 --> 00:08:22,300
Oh, no, this looks delicious.

165
00:08:23,300 --> 00:08:26,359
I sure hope Nami and Robin
appreciate the hard work.

166
00:08:26,460 --> 00:08:28,517
Wow, it doesn't even look like food.

167
00:08:28,600 --> 00:08:31,337
I've never seen such a
beautifully prepared lunch before.

168
00:08:31,420 --> 00:08:32,380
Here. Really?

169
00:08:32,860 --> 00:08:35,440
I made one for you as well. Really?

170
00:08:35,680 --> 00:08:37,280
Custom-made just for me?

171
00:08:37,640 --> 00:08:40,757
I've prepared all the food today
according to a theme I've chosen.

172
00:08:40,840 --> 00:08:45,060
I call it Love is a Cruel Mistress,
Feast for a Fallen Angel. I see.

173
00:08:45,400 --> 00:08:47,341
I don't get what all the fuss is.

174
00:08:47,440 --> 00:08:48,820
It's just a box lunch.

175
00:08:50,500 --> 00:08:52,320
How dare you trash my work!

176
00:08:52,480 --> 00:08:53,817
You better watch your mouth!

177
00:08:53,900 --> 00:08:55,977
A great meal starts
with great presentation!

178
00:08:56,060 --> 00:08:56,890
Why bother?

179
00:08:56,973 --> 00:08:58,397
It all comes out the same.

180
00:08:58,480 --> 00:09:00,437
You're stuffing your face
without even looking!

181
00:09:00,520 --> 00:09:01,360
Yeah, and?

182
00:09:02,940 --> 00:09:05,237
Why are you so mad if
this doesn't taste good?

183
00:09:05,320 --> 00:09:08,849
Because food should please your
eyes as well as your palate.

184
00:09:13,860 --> 00:09:14,690
Hey!

185
00:09:15,980 --> 00:09:17,297
Something's wrong with this ship.

186
00:09:17,380 --> 00:09:18,210
Huh?

187
00:09:19,160 --> 00:09:20,840
What is it? Take a look.

188
00:09:20,980 --> 00:09:22,997
She just started rocking all of a sudden.

189
00:09:23,080 --> 00:09:23,910
Really?

190
00:09:23,993 --> 00:09:28,420
Hope they're not having a party
without us. Hey, look. It's Nami.

191
00:09:30,460 --> 00:09:31,290
Wait.

192
00:09:31,480 --> 00:09:33,951
Why in the world is she wearing a t-shirt?

193
00:09:35,040 --> 00:09:38,393
I'm pretty sure we have more
pressing concerns right now!

194
00:09:38,600 --> 00:09:39,460
Guys, look!

195
00:09:39,620 --> 00:09:41,032
The ship started moving!

196
00:09:41,280 --> 00:09:42,360
But why?

197
00:09:43,420 --> 00:09:46,067
They wouldn't just leave
us here, would they?

198
00:09:46,780 --> 00:09:47,610
Whoa!

199
00:09:48,000 --> 00:09:51,377
I don't think I've ever seen a
ship sailing backwards before!

200
00:09:51,460 --> 00:09:54,560
But they haven't even
set the sails yet! Huh?

201
00:09:56,540 --> 00:09:58,246
There's something underneath!

202
00:10:01,700 --> 00:10:03,641
I think we're being dragged away.

203
00:10:03,960 --> 00:10:05,180
But by what?

204
00:10:07,580 --> 00:10:08,780
It must be.

205
00:10:11,920 --> 00:10:15,600
It's the legendary White White
Sea Super Express monster.

206
00:10:17,420 --> 00:10:19,080
Guys, we're being hijacked.

207
00:10:19,320 --> 00:10:20,908
We'll have to abandon ship.

208
00:10:21,000 --> 00:10:24,237
Come on, we've got to move right
now while we still have time.

209
00:10:24,320 --> 00:10:25,697
We can't leave the ship.

210
00:10:25,780 --> 00:10:27,877
Without it, we won't be
able to get back home.

211
00:10:27,960 --> 00:10:30,200
Then I'll stay behind. Just go now.

212
00:10:30,940 --> 00:10:31,770
Forget it!

213
00:10:31,880 --> 00:10:35,420
You can't defend the whole
ship by yourself! I'll manage!

214
00:10:51,400 --> 00:10:53,300
All right, making progress.

215
00:10:54,480 --> 00:10:56,774
I don't think that'll get you anywhere.

216
00:10:59,020 --> 00:11:00,260
Come back on board.

217
00:11:01,320 --> 00:11:02,320
Why should I?

218
00:11:02,420 --> 00:11:04,677
You'll never be able to
significantly damage that creature,

219
00:11:04,760 --> 00:11:06,197
and we've got bigger problems now.

220
00:11:06,280 --> 00:11:07,380
Look! What?

221
00:11:13,600 --> 00:11:17,247
A school of vicious skyfish are
following us, ready to attack.

222
00:11:17,520 --> 00:11:19,560
We can't jump ship and escape now.

223
00:11:20,720 --> 00:11:22,997
Even if we manage to defeat the skyfish,

224
00:11:23,080 --> 00:11:25,697
I'm sure that more will
arrive to take their place.

225
00:11:25,780 --> 00:11:29,860
Our punishment has already begun,
and there's no way to stop it.

226
00:11:30,420 --> 00:11:31,597
Heaven's judgment.

227
00:11:31,680 --> 00:11:34,377
They must be taking us
to the Forbidden Island.

228
00:11:34,460 --> 00:11:36,342
Guess they got tired of waiting.

229
00:11:36,860 --> 00:11:38,919
Hunter has really got it in for us.

230
00:11:40,020 --> 00:11:40,850
Oh, no.

231
00:11:40,933 --> 00:11:42,880
Please, I can't go back there.

232
00:11:46,600 --> 00:11:47,430
Luffy!

233
00:11:47,513 --> 00:11:48,420
Help us!

234
00:11:48,940 --> 00:11:49,770
Saji!

235
00:12:09,440 --> 00:12:10,340
Why, Nami?

236
00:12:10,600 --> 00:12:11,740
Why a t-shirt?

237
00:12:11,960 --> 00:12:13,537
You're still thinking of that?

238
00:12:13,620 --> 00:12:14,797
This is awful, Luffy.

239
00:12:14,880 --> 00:12:15,710
What are we going to do?

240
00:12:15,793 --> 00:12:17,855
We have to rescue Nami and the others.

241
00:12:18,720 --> 00:12:19,960
Hmm. I wonder.

242
00:12:20,320 --> 00:12:21,555
Where are they going?

243
00:12:21,800 --> 00:12:22,657
Where are they going?

244
00:12:22,740 --> 00:12:23,570
Yes, right.

245
00:12:24,660 --> 00:12:25,580
I got nothing.

246
00:12:27,200 --> 00:12:29,380
Um, well... Huh? Huh?

247
00:12:31,980 --> 00:12:34,940
The Super Express Lobster
is a messenger of Eneru.

248
00:12:35,080 --> 00:12:38,433
He must be taking your friends
as a sacrificial offering.

249
00:12:38,900 --> 00:12:40,180
If that's the case,

250
00:12:40,360 --> 00:12:44,713
they are being taken to the Northeast
Upper Yard to the sacrificial altar.

251
00:12:45,800 --> 00:12:46,780
Say what?

252
00:12:47,040 --> 00:12:49,417
You don't mean that Nami
and Robin and the rest

253
00:12:49,500 --> 00:12:53,800
are going to be sacrificed
to that wannabe god?

254
00:12:54,200 --> 00:12:59,120
That bastard better not harm a
single hair on my pretty Nami's head.

255
00:12:59,940 --> 00:13:04,411
But listen carefully, because I have
not yet told you what else will happen.

